From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: axp20x_battery: PinePhone: Vbus hold voltage 4.5 V

The AXP803 holds Vbus at 4.0 V by default: it keeps drawing until the supply
sags that far. Charging from a PC's USB port, the port gave up first and
power-cycled itself (host: "device descriptor read/64, error -71", "attempt
power cycle"). At 4.5 V the PMIC lowers its input current before the port
collapses, so it charges as fast as the port allows.

Megi's kernel does this in axp20x_usb_power ("Change Vbus hold voltage to
4.5V"), which this firmware does not build (it breaks the USB gadget), so it
goes next to the PinePhone's thermal setup of the previous patch.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
@@ -1186,6 +1186,16 @@
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(axp20x_batt->regmap, 0x84, 0x37, 0x32);
 		if (ret)
 			goto warn_bat;
+
+		/*
+		 * Vbus hold voltage 4.5 V (0x30 bits 5:3, 4.0 V + 0.1 V steps; 4.0 V by
+		 * default): the input current drops before the supply sags below it, so a
+		 * weak USB port is not overloaded until it resets. As Megi's "Change Vbus
+		 * hold voltage to 4.5V" does in axp20x_usb_power, which is not built here.
+		 */
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(axp20x_batt->regmap, 0x30, 0x7 << 3, 0x5 << 3);
+		if (ret)
+			goto warn_bat;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
